  "why": "The Cat and the Dragon (Neko to Ryuu) is a 12 episode summer 2026 run, weekly, ending 2026-09-12 on anilist and kitsu. anizip:19172 is the same run: it carries SAME_AS ids to anilist:186863 and mal:61048 and lists the same 12 episodes under the run's own titles. cr:GT00378117-GS00378133 is the same run: it carries SAME_AS ids to all four members and its 11 listed episodes are the run's first 11 by title, none of them past the run's end. jw:471316-514816 is the same run: it carries SAME_AS ids to all four members and to anizip:19172, and its 11 episode titles match one for one. cr:GT00378117 is the bare Crunchyroll series container for the show, with no dates and no episodes of its own, so it holds the run. nf:81642967 is a different work despite its SAME_AS claims: it is titled Tiger and Dragon, dated 2005-01-01, and its episode list is a prologue followed by eleven generically numbered episodes, which is the 2005 live action drama and not this 2026 anime. Episodes 1 to 11 are paired between anizip, Crunchyroll and JustWatch on exact, distinctive titles in the same order (\"The Kittens and the Winged Uncle\" at 3, \"The Return of the Mother Cat\" at 7, \"The White Cat and the Lazy Girl\" at 9); the anizip dates sit a week after the Crunchyroll dates throughout, matching the catalogues' own split over the start date (2026-06-27 on anilist, kitsu and Crunchyroll, 2026-07-04 on mal and anizip), so the pairing rests on the titles. anizip's episode 12 has no title anywhere and kitsu's twelve episode rows carry neither titles nor dates, so neither is paired."
